drm/amdgpu: set up the register remap on SOC v1.0

soc_v1_0_common_early_init() never calls nbio set_reg_remap(), unlike nv,
soc15, soc21 and soc24, so rmmio_remap.bus_addr stays 0 on GC 12.1. KFD then
refuses ROCr's allocation of the MMIO remap page (AMDKFD_IOC_ALLOC_MEMORY_OF_GPU
returns -ENOMEM) and the thunk fails with "Failed to map remapped mmio page".

Still missing on mainline at the 2026-10-21 drm-next merge.

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/soc_v1_0.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/soc_v1_0.c
@@ -288,6 +288,8 @@
 
 	adev->asic_funcs = &soc_v1_0_asic_funcs;
 
+	adev->nbio.funcs->set_reg_remap(adev);
+
 	adev->rev_id = amdgpu_device_get_rev_id(adev);
 	adev->external_rev_id = 0xff;
 
